abstract: >-
  A practical, opinionated handbook on marketing and go-to-market for
  engineers, technical founders and open-source maintainers. Twenty-nine
  chapters covering positioning, AI search visibility (GEO and AEO),
  developer marketing and DevRel, open-source-led growth, launching,
  community, email deliverability, pricing, analytics and attribution,
  privacy and compliance, and the AI marketing stack. Current for 2026 and
  explicit about which previously standard tactics no longer work.
